From: pas7std co-op <coop@pas7std.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 0010/0010] CONCORD startup rules: the cache hit copied every rule through JSON

buildConfiguredConcordStartupRules already caches by signature, but the hit path
returned cachedRules.map((rule) => cloneValue(rule)) where cloneValue is
JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(...)). Every scene tick that asks for the startup rules
paid a JSON round-trip over the whole generated rule set; a V8 profile of the
running server attributed 1.4% of self time to that clone (and it is the top
stock cost once the NPC store clone is fixed).

structuredClone is the same deep copy for plain JSON data without the stringify
round-trip. No rule, signature or cache semantics change.
Upstream base: c3ea396b6761a0ed3e71ad5b8dd7507f9ae6d69f

diff --git a/server/src/space/npc/npcDefaultConcordRules.js b/server/src/space/npc/npcDefaultConcordRules.js
index daf23f0..c4b2db0 100644
--- a/server/src/space/npc/npcDefaultConcordRules.js
+++ b/server/src/space/npc/npcDefaultConcordRules.js
@@ -271,7 +271,9 @@ function buildConfiguredConcordStartupRules(authoredRules = []) {
 
   const signature = buildSignature(authoredRules);
   if (signature === cachedSignature) {
-    return cachedRules.map((rule) => cloneValue(rule));
+    // structuredClone is the same deep copy without a JSON round-trip; this line
+    // ran for every scene tick that asks for the startup rules.
+    return structuredClone(cachedRules);
   }
 
   const { gateCoveredSystems, stationCoveredSystems } = collectAuthoredCoverage(
